cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHI-Weaver, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PHI-Weaver: AI-assisted ontology-based curation and term suggestion for pathogen-host interactions"
abstract: >-
  A curator-in-the-loop framework that assists PHI-base and PHI-Canto curation
  workflows using large language models. Covers literature intake, ontology term
  lookup and validation (PHIPO, PHIDO, PECO, GO), annotation drafting against
  documented curation standards, and quality checks.
license: MIT  # software; repository content is CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CONTENT)
repository-code: "https://github.com/PHI-base/phi-weaver"
url: "https://github.com/PHI-base/phi-weaver"
keywords:
  - biocuration
  - pathogen-host interactions
  - PHI-base
  - PHI-Canto
  - PHIPO
  - ontology annotation
  - large language models
authors:
  # TODO: confirm the co-author list before this file is published or cited.
  # Candidates from the contribution record: Hsin-Yu Chang (curation standards,
  # validation authority), James Seager (software), Alayne Cuzick. Authorship is
  # a human decision, so only the repo owner is listed here for now.
  - family-names: Urban
    given-names: Martin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: replace placeholder
    affiliation: Rothamsted Research

